  "metric_finding": "Time-to-jam separates the rungs monotonically where the pass count cannot. median onset/expected goes 0.35 -> 0.65 -> 0.86 across sens_a/b/c and agrees with both ASR metrics (wer_med 0.4146 -> 0.3667 -> 0.1143; spoken_med 0.706 -> 0.712 -> 1.0), while the pass count reads 2, 2, 1 and therefore ranks the best rung last. On n=8 the pass count has almost no resolution: it is a count of a disjunction of six gates, and one gate firing hides every other difference. Time-to-jam also costs nothing: it needs the audio envelope and the reference word count, no ASR and no GPU, so it is cheap enough to run on every candidate in a sensitivity sweep rather than on a sample.",
  "caveat": "n=8 units per rung and a single seed. The ORDERING is supported by three independent metrics agreeing, not by any one of them. The magnitudes are not."
